Package: classydms
Type: Package
Title: GC-DMS Disease Classification via Synthetic Pre-Training
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Margaret", "Janiczek", , "TODO@TODO.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Lin", "Cai", , "lcai@umass.edu", role = "ctb"),
    person("Raji", "Balasubramanian", , "rbalasub@umass.edu", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: An end-to-end pipeline for disease vs control classification
    from Gas Chromatography Differential Mobility Spectrometry (GC-DMS)
    data. Includes preprocessing (Savitzky-Golay smoothing, asymmetric
    least squares baseline correction, dust thresholding, occupancy-based
    trimming, normalization, padding), parametric synthetic data
    generation matched to real peak distributions, self-supervised
    denoising-autoencoder pre-training of a convolutional encoder,
    transfer learning via elastic net on the learned features, and
    spatial saliency mapping for biomarker discovery. Designed to support
    small-sample clinical GC-DMS studies (n ~ 100-200 subjects) across
    multiple disease settings.
